ShellUpdate
/ PlangOS (whose %!app.parent% this app is) asks for new files for its shell: what is staged in /shell.next goes down
/ as [{path, content}] — the path where it goes in PlangOS (/system/plangos/desktop.html) — and is removed, so each
/ staged file goes once. Nothing staged: an empty list.
/ Each file is staged with .staged.txt after its name (screen.pr.staged.txt): so it is read as the text it is — a .pr
/ read as itself is a goal, an unknown kind is binary.
- set %update% to []
- set %files% to []
- goal.call(Name="Staged"); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="NothingStaged")])
- foreach %files%, call PackFile file=%item%
- condition.if(Left=%update%, Operator="isnotempty") { file.delete(Path="/shell.next", Recursive=true) }
- return %update%

Staged
- file.list(Path="/shell.next", Recursive=true); variable.set(Name=%files%, Value=%!data%)

NothingStaged
/ no /shell.next: nothing staged
- set %files% to []

PackFile
/ (formal: `as text` is dropped by the builder)
- file.read(Path=%file%); variable.set(Name=%content%, Value=%!data%, Type="text")
/ the path from the shell's folder: /shell.next/.build/screen.pr.staged.txt is .build/screen.pr. %file!relative% is the
/ path from this app's root, written with / on Windows too (%file% itself has \ there)
- variable.set(Name=%relative%, Value=%file!relative%)
- variable.set(Name=%inside%, Value=%relative.replace("/shell.next/", "")%)
- variable.set(Name=%path%, Value=%inside.replace(".staged.txt", "")%)
/ where it goes in PlangOS: the shell's folder, /system/plangos
- add {"path": "/system/plangos/%path%", "content": %content%} to %update%
